# SRAM memory layout. Region sizes, stack placement and the arena minimum.
# The POOL length decides everything downstream: stacks follow it, NOINIT
# follows the stacks. The linker scripts derive addresses from POOL_SIZE.

# kc2mm:label "Memory"

config POOL_SIZE
    hex "POOL region size"
    default 0x74000 if EMU
    default 0x54000
    help
      Size of the POOL SRAM region (big zero-initialised buffers: FX delay
      lines, LVGL heap, canvases, engine arena). FM-1 hardware has 336 KiB
      (0x54000); the emulator exposes 464 KiB (0x74000) from fm1-live's
      larger chip model.

config ARENA_MIN
    hex "Audio arena minimum (bytes)"
    default 0x0 if EMU
    default 0xC000 if CORE_FELUCCA
    default 0x22C00
    help
      The linker asserts that the working arena (the POOL tail after statics
      and code) is at least this large. Felucca uses fixed buffers (48 KiB
      is enough for the four largest engine states); Melodee's allocator
      needs 139 KiB. Set to 0 for emulator builds (no real-time audio).
